"""Render the cohort report from sealed-stage summaries."""
from summarize_broader_geometry import OUT,read,run


def report():
    result=run(); rows=result['cases']; by={r['name']:r for r in rows}
    text=['## Decision question','',
        'Does the complete V4 production architecture generalize across a broader mixed-geometry cohort that exercises ordinary prism growth, local correction, compression, termination/remesh, mixed shell topology, core generation/repair, complete-mesh qualification, and frozen numerical replay where authoritative CFD controls exist?','']
    def section(title,body):text.extend(['### '+title,'',body,''])
    section('A. Authority verification',
        'Base HEAD: e63b35cfb67465ae209b844526d107a4fc3d1ff5. COHORT_MANIFEST.json binds each geometry source to its preserved authority. The SF2 numerical report SHA-256 is e6611d2b73b0c37a339e915a7ce455d2f7a14210295322948547a8874db73c89; authority SHA-256 is 3aec6f000c76a3f48d9f86764a80c8336cf018394961ea9b7c772d6777eaf4b0. No sealed source, mesh gate, certificate method, trigger policy, shell geometry, or V3 file was changed.')
    table=['| Case | Scope | Shell cells | Core tets | Complete cells | Complete geometry |',
        '|---|---|---:|---:|---:|---|']
    for r in rows:
        table.append(f"| {r['name']} | {r['scope']} | {r['shell_cells']:,} | {r.get('core',{}).get('tets',1597714):,} | {r['complete_cells'] if r['complete_cells'] is not None else 'not qualified'} | {'pass' if r['complete_passed'] else 'FAIL: frozen shell determinant'} |")
    section('B. Cohort design','\n'.join(table)+'\n\nSix distinct geometries are counted. SF2 is the sole full production domain. Five cases are bounded domains. The wide cavity has 10,240 shell cells and a large exact-proof population, but is not evidence of a second large production domain. Checkpoints and A/B repeats are not extra geometries.')
    text.extend(['Git review: GIT_REVIEW.json lists all committed paths. They are V4-only. V3 modification count is zero. All 155 unrelated dirty path entries remain. Two existing nested-checkout status markers changed from M to m during the run; no task operation modified those checkouts. Raw Windows log bytes are preserved; source whitespace checks pass with CR recognized as a line ending.',''])
    section('C. Geometry authorities',
        'GEOMETRY_AUTHORITY.json records wall/source identity, binary64 schedule, h1, adjusted schedules, and local layer distribution for each bounded case. h1 remains 0.000166527069 m. The shared native MixedFrontRunner uses the existing qualified fixture provider; the general-SDF case uses the existing historical adjusted-schedule provider. Source-keyed outer-interface extraction is shared. Case names select immutable inputs, not production decisions.\n\nFresh bounded runs construct the preserved pre-trigger shell, then execute remesh and continuation in the native transaction loop. They are not fresh layer-0 production searches. SF2 uses a fresh bounded native replay of the qualified full shell and a fresh Foundation precheck; its full build and numerical A/A2 are reused sealed evidence.')
    section('D. Ordinary-growth controls',
        'SF2 and the wide spherical cavity perform zero remesh events. The wide cavity advances from its valid layer-19 state to layer 20 through the native runner. SF2 retains all 20 layers, exact atlas/forecast state, and all quality/certificate receipts.')
    section('E. Steerable-warning cases',
        'SF2 supplies the qualified steerable-warning and ordinary-correction history. The fresh native replay preserves its correction state and zero-remesh outcome. No new active search was run on SF2 and no accepted correction coordinates were presented as a fresh search result.')
    section('F. Compression/redistribution cases',
        'The general-SDF run preserves its adjusted/compressed local schedule, actual offsets, local last-prism map, and subsequent rollback. It removes 45 committed layer-4 prisms and two layer-5 tetrahedra, then commits layer-6 continuation. This repairs already-committed problematic upper geometry; it does not prove prevention of the historical commit. This is one adjusted-schedule shell pass. An independent complete compression-only/no-remesh control is not established. Complete general-SDF assembly fails the frozen shell-coupling gate described below.')
    section('G. Termination/remesh cases',
        'General-SDF, narrowing channel, curved passage, and spherical capacity cases each trigger one automatic remesh and commit a subsequent prism continuation step. All four shell paths pass. Triggers use current qualified evidence; no fixture IDs enter the trigger policy. The three latter cases also pass complete bounded geometry. General-SDF does not.')
    section('H. Capacity-limited cases',
        'The analytic spherical capacity case commits remesh and layer-14 continuation. Its two disconnected fluid cavities are both meshed. A real adapter defect was repaired: the historical helper extracted volume 1 only. The new shared extraction iterates all volume entities, sorts scientific node/tet tags, and rejects unsupported element types. No surface coordinate or mesh-science control changed.')
    section('I. Mixed-shell topology',
        'The qualified bounded assemblies contain prism-, pyramid-, and tet-owned interface faces. Explicit terminated columns stay out of the prism-advance front. Source ownership, wall identity, first-layer identity, and native checkpoint identity remain exact. Neither the core adapter nor assembly assumes every shell face is a prism top.')
    blocker=by['general_asymmetric_passage']['blocker']['failures'][0]
    section('J. Shell quality',
        f"Standalone shell validation passes all bounded runs. Complete coupling exposes a real scientific obstruction in general-SDF shell tetrahedron {blocker['scientific_cell']}, source {blocker['source']}, layer {blocker['layer']}. Its standalone determinant is {blocker['standalone_determinant']:.17g}; with all four faces coupled it is {blocker['complete_determinant']:.17g}, below 0.0011. Independent 70-digit arithmetic gives {blocker['high_precision_complete']}.\n\nThe former coupled-face mask is [false,true,true,true]. Core attachment makes all four faces internal. The determinant depends only on the frozen shell face-area tensor. Interior-core vertex repair cannot change it. Making the interface external would violate conformality. The case stops at this gate. No shell movement, threshold change, or complete-mesh publication was attempted. The small exact reproducer is FIXED_SHELL_COUPLING_OBSTRUCTION.json. Prior bounded core/interface checks did not establish this complete coupled-shell gate.")
    section('K. Shell certificates',
        '\n'.join(f"- {r['name']}: {r['shell_relations']:,} preserved valid shell relations." for r in rows)+
        '\n\nNew complete certificates reuse unchanged shell dependency-bound proofs. Shell passes do not override the separate complete quality failure.')
    text.extend([f"Cohort shell-touching interpolation-weight minimum: {result['extrema']['shell_touching_weight_min']:.17g}. The lowest shell determinant including the failed complete assembly is {result['extrema']['worst_shell_determinant_including_failed_assembly']:.17g}.",''])
    section('L. Outer-interface qualification',
        'One source-keyed adapter supplies coordinates, ordered faces, ownership, and ancestry for all cases. Core extraction checks exact binary64 boundary coordinates and exact boundary-face recovery. Complete assembly checks owner/neighbour incidence and winding. Passed assemblies have zero missing faces, duplicates, gaps, or overlaps. General-SDF interface recovery also passes, but complete hard quality does not. All current core-facing facets are triangles. Arbitrary polygon triangulation and nested domains with mixed orientation are not qualified by this cohort; the adapter rejects unsupported inputs.')
    section('M. Core generation',
        'The same bounded Gmsh Delaunay route uses preserved sizing and three standard optimization passes. Outward components use the existing bounded envelope; inward components form enclosed fluid volumes. Orientation selects domain topology, not fixture identity. These envelopes do not establish CFD boundary conditions. All five fresh cores pass their applicable frozen core and shell/core face gates. GENERATION.json records exact extrema, counts, time, and RSS.')
    section('N. Core repair',
        'No fresh bounded core requires repair. SF2 retains the sealed repair of four interior vertices with unchanged connectivity and fixed interface. The general-SDF failure belongs to the shell, not core quality. Further interior-core repair cannot alter its controlling determinant; no pointless optimization was used to conceal that obstruction.')
    text.extend([f"Across fresh bounded cores and reused SF2 authority, minimum core determinant is {result['extrema']['core_determinant_min']:.17g}; minimum core interpolation weight is {result['extrema']['core_weight_min']:.17g}.",''])
    section('O. Complete assembly',
        '\n'.join(f"- {r['name']}: "+(f"{r['complete_cells']:,} cells; {r['complete_relations']:,} complete relations; pass." if r['complete_passed'] else 'stopped before complete certification; frozen shell determinant fails.') for r in rows)+
        '\n\nFresh bounded passes require complete mixed quality, positive cells, ownership, exact volume balance/interior degree, and all required new continuous relations. SF2 counts are reused from sealed complete authority. Passing core quality alone is never treated as a complete pass.')
    section('P. Foundation 13 qualification',
        'SF2 was checked again in the qualified numerical case. Exit 0 and literal `Mesh OK.` pass. The first mesh-only copy lacked controlDict; that infrastructure reproducer is preserved, and the valid sealed numerical case supplied unchanged controls. Fresh successful precheck: 100.35 s, 3,595,124,736 bytes peak RSS. The bounded fixtures use the strongest applicable complete geometric qualification; Foundation/CFD cases were not invented for them. Fresh Foundation pass count: one.')
    section('Q. Numerical A/A2 qualification',
        'One qualified numerical case is reused: SF2. A/A2 both OuterConverged, 50 solves each, 8,839 PCG iterations each, maximum 659, two consecutive complete passes, exact observers and replay. Normalized global flux imbalance is 1.5037983906771337e-13; wall flux is zero. Diagnostic fvc::flux(U)-q L2 is 0.0020264342486056236 and Linf is 2.3130845471315356. No fresh A/A2 solve is claimed in this task.')
    section('R. Numerical cases not evaluated',
        'Five bounded cases have no authoritative geometry-bound CFD boundary conditions and physical observers. Existing V3 numerical controls were inspected, but bind different historical domains. Assigning those controls would invent scientific authority. NUMERICAL_AUTHORITY_AUDIT.json records this boundary. The requested numerical coverage beyond SF2 is not established. Spatial convergence and general CFD accuracy are not established by this cohort.')
    section('S. Trigger false-positive/false-negative audit',
        str(result['trigger_audit'])+'\n\nAll four expected remesh shell cases trigger. Both negative controls do not. General-SDF complete assembly failure is not a missed remesh trigger. Unevaluated stages are not counted as trigger passes.')
    section('T. Cross-case mechanism analysis',
        'Ordinary growth, steerable correction history, adjusted schedules, current-evidence remesh, source-keyed mixed front, disconnected cavity core extraction, and native restart work across the measured subset. The new limitation is coupled-shell quality after core insertion. It is a geometry/gate obstruction in one bounded class, not permission to change mesh science. Other repaired plumbing defects were optional psutil import on WSL, reporting a column status under the wrong key, release of mmap owners before Windows temporary cleanup, cyclic face-start normalization, and resolving nominal schedule authority by its exact stored hash.')
    perf=['| Case | Fresh shell/replay s | Core s | Assembly s | Shell/replay peak bytes |', '|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
    for r in rows:
        perf.append(f"| {r['name']} | {r['performance']['seconds']:.3f} | {r.get('core',{}).get('seconds',0):.3f} | {(r.get('assembly') or {}).get('seconds',0):.3f} | {r['performance']['peak_rss_bytes']:,} |")
    section('U. Runtime and memory','\n'.join(perf)+'\n\nZero in the core/assembly columns for SF2 means reused, not free execution. General-SDF has no successful complete-assembly time. Raw logs preserve rejected attempts and separate replay time. The wide control expands bounded exact proof records; it is slower and more memory-heavy than the optimized SF2 production proof path. No global dense optimizer, new scientific precision, or memory acceptance threshold was introduced. Prior SF2 A/A2 times and peak RSS remain historical, not fresh task measurements.')
    slowest=max(result['fresh_case_stage_seconds'],key=result['fresh_case_stage_seconds'].get)
    text.extend([f"Maximum fresh task peak RSS: {result['maximum_fresh_peak_rss_bytes']:,} bytes. Slowest fresh A path: {slowest}, {result['fresh_case_stage_seconds'][slowest]:.3f} s including shell, core, and successful assembly. The wide shell alone used 2,993.051 s and peaked at 5,612,032,000 bytes. Its measured proposal phase was 882.594 s and validation phase 866.234 s. Code inspection shows repeated full bounded certification and retained initial evidence; no allocation-class profiling or scalable-memory qualification is claimed for that provider.",''])
    section('V. Determinism',
        'Curved passage, spherical capacity, and narrowing channel fresh A/B shell scientific hashes match. Their core arrays match exactly. General-SDF and the wide control have source-keyed geometry reconstruction, native checkpoint replay, and independent core replay. SF2 native atlas, forecast, receipt/certificate and interface replay are exact. These bounded replay scopes are recorded explicitly; no unexecuted fresh full-shell search is claimed.')
    section('W. Tests',
        '11 focused cohort unittest tests pass. They cover all-volume extraction, deterministic ordering, unsupported core elements, connected interface components, trigger counts with missing cases, and the coupled-shell determinant reproducer. 82 retained pytest tests pass: native core interface, fixed-interface repair, mixed front, and termination policy. Scientific runs and failures are separate from unit tests. See tests.stdout/tests.stderr and retained_tests.stdout/retained_tests.stderr.')
    section('X. Classification',
        '**V4BroaderMixedGeometryEndToEndPartiallyQualified**. The successful complete subset is broad, but general-SDF complete assembly fails a frozen scientific gate. Five numerical cases lack authoritative controls. The independent compression-only complete control, second large production domain, and numerical coverage beyond SF2 remain unestablished. This is not a full cohort or CFD qualification.')
    section('Y. Production claim supported by evidence',
        result['claim']+' Native production authority and automatic remesh defaults remain unchanged. The newly discovered general-SDF coupled-shell failure must block reuse of that complete mesh.')
    section('Z. Recommended next task',result['next_task']+' After that, broader geometry-family qualification is appropriate before any broad CFD claim. No next task was implemented.')
    (OUT/'report.md').write_text('\n'.join(text))


if __name__=='__main__':report()
